{"schema":"LAW_EN_DOCUMENT_V1","id":"i18n-202eeae2d29da00c0c5ade18eae7c80306a1d21075b9e6f6","family_id":"KR:012159","country":"KR","language":"en","title":"Special Act on Investigating the Truth of the April 16 Sewol Ferry Disaster and Building a Safe Society","title_original":"4ㆍ16세월호참사 진상규명 및 안전사회 건설 등을 위한 특별법","kind":"법률","source_version":"284117","promulgated":null,"effective":null,"translation_status":"AI_DRAFT","body_status":"BODY_LOADED","source_url":"https://www.law.go.kr/LSW/lsInfoP.do?lsiSeq=284117","source_sha256":"c141291f23520264444e31f7c7002ae169ff7b5f49b50f81aade863d8c364da6","body_sha256":"88f3f8f8b00d6371d4c57983a5910f0bc06bbad9d1a55b26f46e07ce877fcae1","article_count":1,"full_text":"Article 34 (Oaths of Witnesses, etc.) (1) Where the Chairperson of the Inquest requires a witness or appraiser attending a hearing, to present testimony or appraisal, he/she shall have the witness or appraiser take an oath. \n  (2) Where any person who attends a hearing as a reference witness agrees to take an oath as a witness, he/she may be examined as a witness. \n  (3) The Chairperson of the Inquest shall clearly state the meaning of an oath before the oath, and inform the relevant person of the punishment for false testimony or appraisal.\n  (4) Where any person takes an oath as a witness under paragraphs (1) and (2), Article 157 of the Criminal Procedure Act shall apply mutatis mutandis.  \n  (5) Where any person takes an oath as an appraiser under paragraph (1), Article 170 of the Criminal Procedure Act shall apply mutatis mutandis.\n","metadata":{"author_method":"Exact held-source units translated or completed using explicitly recorded source/target spans; original official records remain unchanged. All new units are MACHINE_TRANSLATION and UNREVIEWED.","author_title_record":{"path":"D:\\lawsofkorea\\projece\\07_법률번역\\06_법령별다국어완성\\LAW12_20261018_1442\\workc_1129_2094\\review_pending\\WORKC_G01_P04\\1525_KR012159\\translations\\act\\en.title.json","sha256":"4c74a